{
  "$template": "@atlante/pack/skill",
  "description": "Use when initializing, configuring, validating, building, troubleshooting, or improving an Atlante harness.",
  "title": "Harness",
  "overview": "Operate an Atlante harness with evidence: initialize and configure it from repository facts, run harness-related delivery alongside the active workflow phases, and route observed friction into a separately approved improvement cycle. This is a stewardship capability, not a workflow phase.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "markdown": "## Operating context\n\nTreat this skill as a supplement to the active workflow phases (`brainstorm`, `plan`, `build`, `review`); it operates alongside them rather than replacing them or adding a fifth phase. Keep permanent policy authoritative and command-level mechanics provisional: mechanics are the first content shed when verified deterministic tools (such as a future Atlante MCP server) provide the same operations, and exact tool schemas, effects, and diagnostics belong in tool descriptions rather than here.\n\n### Atlante concepts\n\nAn Atlante harness is defined by authored source configuration and realized through built artifacts:\n\n- `atlante.jsonc` is the project's root source configuration. It declares values, agents, skills, and other bindings; `extends` inherits a preset such as `@atlante/pack`.\n- Values are named interpolations resolved into documents and rendered output; the first-party preset defines `project` and `workflow-root`.\n- Agents are rendered prompts that own a workflow; skills are project-global Markdown guidance an agent loads on demand through the host adapter's skill tool.\n- Templates define input structure and rendering; instances bind a template to concrete input. Versioned presets and packs are installable bundles of templates and instances.\n- Bindings connect named configuration entries to templates or instances.\n- Built artifacts are the deterministic rendered outputs published under the artifact tree and verified before a host adapter materializes them.\n\nDistinguish authoritative source configuration from generated output at all times: source configuration and project sources are the editable surface, and generated output is reproduced through validated build or materialization.\n\n### Coverage areas\n\n| Coverage area | Disposition |\n| --- | --- |\n| Atlante concepts and document structure, including the source-versus-generated boundary | Permanent policy |\n| Choosing suitable first-party, local, or package resources without inventing unavailable ones | Permanent policy |\n| Recognizing recurring workflow friction and proposing a separately approved harness-improvement cycle | Permanent policy |\n| Initializing Atlante and creating or updating `atlante.jsonc` from repository evidence | Provisional mechanics |\n| Running validation and build or materialization commands and interpreting common diagnostics | Provisional mechanics |\n| Integrating and troubleshooting the OpenCode adapter from repository evidence | Provisional mechanics |"
    },
    {
      "instructions": [
        "Establish from repository evidence whether Atlante is initialized and which version and capabilities are available before recommending anything; when Atlante is absent or its version or capabilities cannot be established, report that plainly and proceed from what is verified.",
        "Treat the CLI as the universal cold-start bootstrap path; an Atlante-materialized skill becomes available only after the harness and host expose it, so bootstrap guidance starts from the CLI rather than from a materialized skill.",
        "Inspect repository structure, conventions, installed packs, existing resources, project instructions, and desired workflows before recommending configuration; explain suitable choices and help the developer define an approved initialization or configuration task.",
        "Recommend only commands, keys, locators, and resources verified as available to the project; distinguish verified recommendations from unverified suggestions.",
        "Treat current Atlante source configuration and built artifacts as part of the operating environment, distinguishing authoritative source configuration from generated output.",
        "Validate and build or materialize through capabilities verified from the project, reporting diagnostics and unavailable checks truthfully and separating evidenced outcomes from assumptions.",
        "Preserve the phase boundaries and workflow invariants already in force; harness stewardship runs alongside the active phases rather than inside them.",
        "Record material harness friction without silently expanding the current task.",
        "Turn observed workflow friction into an evidence-based suggestion that names the expected benefit and the affected configuration or resources.",
        "Ask the developer before beginning any harness change, and run an accepted improvement as a separate workflow cycle using the normal adaptive brainstorm, plan, build, review, approval, and validation policy.",
        "Present unapproved suggestions as suggestions; an improvement discussed during unrelated work remains unimplemented until its own cycle completes with evidence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "invariants": [
        "MUST NOT direct edits to generated artifacts; direct all changes to authoritative source configuration and reproduce generated output through validated build or materialization.",
        "MUST NOT invent unavailable resources, configuration keys, commands, tool capabilities, or host behavior; report what is verified and what is unavailable.",
        "MUST obtain explicit developer approval before changing the harness or expanding an unrelated task into harness work, and MUST run an accepted improvement as its own delivery cycle.",
        "MUST NOT report an initialization, validation, build, or materialization outcome without command or tool evidence for it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "markdown": "## Resources\n\nStable entry points for orientation. The guidance above stands alone without network access; these links are supplementary for humans and web-capable agents:\n\n- Documentation root: <https://docs.atlante.sh>\n- Getting-started guide: <https://docs.atlante.sh/getting-started>\n- Specification: <https://github.com/atlante/atlante/blob/main/SPECIFICATION.md>\n- JSON Schema: <https://atlante.sh/schema/v0.1/schema.json>"
    }
  ]
}
